  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="d4a3751a-49bb-5d0d-b405-5da60f448657" activityNameId="fbfec83e-243d-5ae9-979c-339288928309" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xxx Window frame, wood-metal, U=1.6 W/m2K, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xxx Window frame, wood-metal, U=1.6 W/m2K, at plant
This dataset describes all the processes and material inputs needed to produce a wood-metal (steel) window frame with 1 m2 visible area. 1 m2 of visible wooden window frame weighs 83.4 kg. \nGeography: Window frames produced and sold in Switzerland and Germany.\nTechnology: The dataset describes highly automated technology processes in window frame manufacturing.\nVersion: 2.2\nEnergy values: Undefined\nLocal category: Bauteile\nLocal subcategory: Fenster\nUVEK 2022 source file:07147.XML\n\n
UUID: 97cd58ba-b91e-3a4c-9960-88f21536a425
Included processes are timber sawing, varnishing (primer, solvents, paint), section bar rolling for steel fittings, joining, fitting, all the road transport at different production phases and the disposal of the paint remains.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: The dataset describes highly automated technology processes in window frame manufacturing.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Company documentation, measurements 
Extrapolations: see Geography
Uncertainty adjustments: The assumption that this dataset is representative for whole Europe is taken into account in the uncertainties.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_97cd58ba-b91e-3a4c-9960-88f21536a425.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
